r-before-outer order. A standalone push defines the acquired FR-219 commit lock as the inner layer of its complete rebase transaction lock: failure to release either layer therefore satisfies the unchanged v2 precondition “Rebase lock could not be explicitly released after the primary outcome was recorded.” Recovery retains the common portable owner while it uses FR-219's serialized ownership/stale-owner protocol to prove and release the exact commit-lock layer first, updates and fsyncs `lock_release`, and only then releases the common layer. A foreign/live/replaced identity is never removed; the record and outer owner remain fail-closed for a later recovery. When both releases are proven, recovery clears `lock_release` with the primary fields and restores the ordinary primary tuple. Outside `lock-release-failed`, any non-null `lock_release` is schema-invalid.\ndocs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md:919:- **FR-103** (MUST): Evaluation is two distinct fail-closed layers. Every control-class candidate MUST run Recorded-baseline integrity over the complete committed `.forge/evals/tasks/` suite; that layer proves only fixture/result presence, grammar, immutability, and equality. When the exact DM-012 staged path set matches any positive pathspec in the `reviewer-facing-eval-triggers` region loaded from the candidate's authenticated base-policy SHA, the same chain MUST additionally obtain fresh, independent judgments for every supported review-role fixture from the candidate tree's fixed known-oracle-free projection, under the candidate route and FR-149 bounds. The fresh manifest MUST bind the v2 authorization ID, object format/tree, base commit, review-diff digest/count, chain ID, one-time request ID, trigger evidence, projection definition and digest, complete fixture inventory, route, process completion, and verdict artifacts; any absence, malformation, stale/foreign binding, unavailable reviewer, or expected/actual mismatch blocks the candidate. A baseline PASS, CI result, prior candidate result, or binding Gate-3 PASS MUST NOT substitute for this fresh layer, and the fresh layer MUST NOT substitute for review-final or candidate-bound operator approval.\ndocs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md:1323:Where `flock` is available, the portable-arbiter owner then opens the owner-controlled regular file `agent-rebase.lock`, polls for an exclusive kernel lock within the same single 300-second deadline, and after acquisition rewrites/fsyncs that file with the same canonical owner record; the complete common lock requires both layers. Where `flock` is unavailable, the portable arbiter alone is complete. The order is always portable arbiter then optional `flock`, and release is optional `flock` then portable arbiter; no entrant holds `flock` while waiting for the portable namespace or ever treats `flock` alone as complete. Thus a Linux entrant and macOS entrant contend on the same no-replace inode namespace, while `flock` remains a secondary compatibility layer rather than a separate lock backend. A non-crash failure before complete acquisition releases only optional kernel ownership and portable names proven to be that invocation's inode, fsyncs each affected directory, and retries within the one deadline; an unmatched name is never removed.\ndocs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md:1327:All stale-portable-owner and dead-fence recovery uses the separate immutable reservation `<git-common-dir>/agent-rebase.recover`: a proven-dead portable owner with no fence, a proven-dead portable owner plus dead-but-published FR-236 fence, and a current mandatory-portable owner that also holds exclusive Linux `flock` but finds a legacy/anomalous dead fence preventing complete admission. After read-only proof of the applicable same-host PID/PGID absence, a contender creates a complete mode-0600 same-directory temporary regular file containing one DM-013-canonical record with exactly `schema`, `recovery_kind`, `host`, `pid`, `nonce`, `started_at`, `stale_owner_inode`, `stale_owner_digest`, `stale_owner_host`, `stale_owner_pid`, `stale_owner_kind`, `stale_owner_chain_id`, `inflight_inode`, `inflight_digest`, `inflight_host`, `inflight_pgid`, `inflight_owner_kind`, `inflight_chain_id`, `owner_dead_at`, and `group_dead_at`. It writes and fsyncs the file, publishes its inode by a no-replace hard link at the reservation path, fsyncs the common directory, unlinks the temporary name, and fsyncs again. `schema` is `forge-rebase-recovery/1`, `recovery_kind` is exactly `fallback-owner`, `fallback-owner-and-fence`, or `flock-held-dead-fence` (the labels remain schema literals although the portable owner is now universal), and the nonce has the same 128-bit grammar. In either `fallback-*` mode `stale_owner_inode`, digest, host, PID, kind, and `owner_dead_at` are non-null; `stale_owner_chain_id` is non-null exactly when that kind is `merge` and is null for `push` or `phase5`. In `flock-held-dead-fence` mode every stale-owner field plus `owner_dead_at` is null because the contender owns the current portable and kernel layers. Every in-flight field plus `group_dead_at` is null in `fallback-owner` mode. In either fence mode `inflight_inode`, digest, host, PGID, kind, and `group_dead_at` are non-null; `inflight_chain_id` is non-null exactly for kind `merge` and null for kind `push`.\ndocs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md:1847:| `recovery_required/lock-release-failed`; release recovery proves the pending inner then outer layers released | recorded primary state/condition/outcome | Clear `lock_release` and the three primary fields and restore DM-017's exact primary tuple, active nonce, and attempt ledger without repeating it. If the restored primary tuple is under invalid committed mode, the hook admits only the applicable recovery-only classification or release completion and the invocation stops with that row's exact result; otherwise apply the ordinary classification/observation row |\nDIFF_EXIT:0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
