t# are ignored here so the contract tracks today's shape. TODO: remove each ignore\n   173\t# once the cross-link is gone (runtime.py:74 is the mirror-image lazy import from\n   174\t# forge_cli into codex_orchestrator; it is not covered by this contract).\n   175\t[[tool.importlinter.contracts]]\n   176\tname = \"codex_orchestrator does not import forge_cli\"\n   177\ttype = \"forbidden\"\n   178\tsource_modules = [\"codex_orchestrator\"]\n   179\tforbidden_modules = [\"forge_cli\"]\n   180\tignore_imports = [\n   181\t    \"codex_orchestrator.builders -> forge_cli.candidate\",\n   182\t    \"codex_orchestrator.builders -> forge_cli.fresh_evals\",\n   183\t    \"codex_orchestrator.builders -> forge_cli.policy\",\n   184\t    \"codex_orchestrator.journal -> forge_cli.chain_core\",\n   185\t]\n   110\t- `codex_orch_tools.py validate --gates` — Level B gate enforcement profile\n   111\t- Plugin PreToolUse hook (`scripts/forge/commit-guard.sh`) — inspects matched Git/Forge command segments that traverse the model's registered Bash-tool path and denies them on halt or missing authorization; it is not a repository-native Git hook and is not an exhaustive claim about every same-user execution path\n   112\t- Plugin PostToolUse hook (`scripts/forge/invariant-guard.sh`) — advisory invariant feedback after Edit/Write\n   113\t- Plugin Stop/SessionStart hooks — the Stop union of telemetry aggregation plus a drift-staleness nudge, and the SessionStart drift-staleness nudge, in forge-initialized repos\n   114\t- `agents/review-final.md` — instruction-bounded, execution-capable Claude reviewer with a binding verdict; it has no Edit/Write tools but shares the orchestrator's writable worktree, so its no-write boundary is not an OS sandbox\n   115\t- `scripts/forge/{check-halt.sh,acquire-commit-lock.sh,release-commit-lock.sh,run-evals.sh,invariant-guard.sh,configure-dcg.sh,drift-check.sh,drift-staleness.sh,aggregate-telemetry.sh,commit-guard.sh,install.sh}` and `scripts/forge/{check-test-quality.py,archive-run.py,audit-commitments.py,emit-decision-event.py,journal-patterns.py}` — executable governance script surfaces\n   116\t- `scripts/forge/run-scoped-mutation.py` — Python-interpreter-loaded governance helper (the merge path invokes it as `python3 <path>` and the drift path imports it), so it is outside the executable-script inventory\n   117\t- `scripts/forge/forge_cli/` — the Python-interpreter-loaded package the Forge CLI is being split into (bead forge-plugin-95e): `scripts/forge/cli.py` remains the sole invoked entry point and shim that FR-221's matcher and the FR-223 corpora pin; the shim puts its own directory on `sys.path`, re-imports the envelope and policy names by explicit named lists, and forwards attribute reads of every `runtime`, `chain_core`, `engine`, and `app` `__all__` export through a module `__getattr__` (PEP 562), so every historical module attribute stays resolvable while tests reach the package through one shared loader (`tests/_cli_loader.py`); no file under it is executable, and it is outside the executable-script inventory exactly as `run-scoped-mutation.py` is. The package holds `envelope.py` (reason codes, `Refusal`, `FrozenError`, `Outcome`), `policy.py` (the committed-policy parser, whose fence helpers are the canonical patch seams), `runtime.py` (the one canonical module for the patchable controls — the clock, the bounded process runner, the merge lifecycle flag, the Revision-9 state controls, the path roots, the lazily imported coordination modules, the fast-tier mechanical-skip predicate, and the late-bound journal-record builder seam — which every module of the split reads by attribute so one in-memory patch on `forge_cli.runtime` disables a control everywhere), `candidate.py` (the shared bounded, pinned Git-context implementation for immutable tree snapshots, deterministic review evidence, marker identity, and raw produced-commit inspection), `chain_core.py` (the fenced process runner, the FR-235 common-lock arbiter and chain leases, chain and merge-chain storage, merge state and transition validation, the ingest verifiers, and the Revision-9 seam-marker loop beside `register_coordination_seams`), `engine.py` (the commit-chain engine, argument-parser construction, finalize pipeline, review/approval/secret-scan helpers, archive surface, merge admission/scope/claim helpers, and Revision-12 bootstrap child protocol; it binds the journal-record builder onto the runtime seam at import), and `app.py` (`MergeEngine`, the shared chain-verb router, argument-parsing and dispatch entry points, and `main`; it obtains the parser and other engine helpers through `forge_cli.engine`). The existing FR-230 phase-3/4 manifest retains its historical production subjects; every changed or added production subject, including `candidate.py`, requires a current applicable Recorded-baseline integrity (`strict-evals`) result binding, plus `fresh-reviewer-evals` when the authenticated-base trigger matches; an unverifiable trigger blocks through its required INVALID path. The split changes no verb, diagnostic, reason code, `--help` byte, or immutable prior corpus.\n   118\t- `scripts/forge/forge_cli/fresh_evals.py` — the non-executable, Python-interpreter-loaded internal collector and verifier for candidate-bound fresh reviewer evaluation; behind the chain-owned `engine.py` launcher adapter it implements authenticated trigger derivation, candidate-tree fixture inventory and oracle withholding, bounded native child execution, canonical request-bound artifacts, manifest verification, and the current-candidate PASS predicate without adding a second CLI entry point\n   119\t- `scripts/forge/cli.py` — the Forge CLI commit-chain slice (FR-210..FR-224): a persisted chain state machine invoked as `python3 \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/forge/cli.py\" <verb>`, owning commit-chain sequencing, staging, candidate identity, evidence capture, and finalize. No PATH binary named `forge` is installed (the Foundry `forge` collision); `forge <verb>` anywhere in this spec is shorthand for that invocation form. Phase-gated: ships only after the FR-223 precondition evals pass\n   120\t- Phase-3 Forge CLI merge surfaces specified by FR-230..FR-237: `status`, `merge start|refresh|verify|gate run|approve|finalize|recover|cleanup|abort`, and the shared `review request|attach|disposition` verbs. These are normative future surfaces, not implementation delivered by Revision 7.\n   121\t- Phase-4 `forge push`, DM-015 activation parsing, and the v2 PreToolUse matcher/raw-denial behavior specified by FR-238..FR-241. These are normative future surfaces, not implementation delivered by Revision 7.\n   122\t- Additive phase-3/4 v2 reason-code and hook-vector artifacts in the exact DM-016 inventory. Every v1 artifact remains immutable.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
